        "official_name": "Open Source Vulnerability Schema",
        "common_name": "OSV Schema",
        "alternate_names": [
          "OSV Format",
          "OpenSSF OSV Schema"
        ],
        "description": "Distributed vulnerability JSON format and schema for open source ecosystems, maintained by the OpenSSF Vulnerability Disclosures Working Group.",
        "notes": "Used by OSV.dev, GitHub Security Advisories (GHSA), Go vulndb, RustSec, PyPA, and other open source advisory databases. Each release tag in github.com/ossf/osv-schema publishes a normative JSON Schema at validation/schema.json.\n\nNote on versioning: version_required is false because the schema version IS the subpath identifier (e.g., #1.9.2 or #1.3). Two-part minor series labels (e.g., 1.9, 1.3) resolve as aliases to the latest patch release in that series both via @version and #subpath.",
        "version_required": false,
